WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.329
It was a beautiful day in First City, and the streets buzzed with energy.

2
00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:24.682
At the edge of Treeview Park, the king and queen of Magica were speaking to a large gathering.

3
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:33.619
Angry people held banners and signs. Some signs were magical, with flashing messages that changed words or colors.

4
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.701
Others were plain signs written by hand.

5
00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:45.450
There had been many protests lately, and now the king and queen were trying to calm down the crowd.

6
00:00:45.451 --> 00:00:50.258
A square-jawed man watched from a balcony overlooking the park.

7
00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:56.634
His big hands rested on a railing, and a door behind him was open to an opulent apartment.

8
00:00:56.635 --> 00:01:02.431
"Void rights," he muttered. "What a concept. Seems popular though."

9
00:01:02.432 --> 00:01:08.649
Suddenly he gasped, his knees buckling as his head exploded with pain.

10
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:14.568
Pressing his hands to his head, he staggered through the door and collapsed onto a sofa.

11
00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:19.987
A moment later the pain faded, and his eyes opened wide with surprise.

12
00:01:19.988 --> 00:01:25.546
"Who is this?" he exclaimed. "How are you—?"

13
00:01:25.547 --> 00:01:31.656
He paused, listening to a voice only he could hear. Then he nodded.

14
00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:36.107
"Yes, of course I remember you. Who could forget?"

15
00:01:36.108 --> 00:01:41.368
He barked out a short, humorless laugh. "But I thought you were dead!

16
00:01:41.369 --> 00:01:44.948
That crazy old woman told the palace that she was going to . . ."

17
00:01:44.949 --> 00:01:49.592
His words trailed off and he cocked his head, listening again.

18
00:01:49.593 --> 00:01:55.371
"Yes, I see," he said. "Well, I'm glad.

19
00:01:55.372 --> 00:01:59.259
I've missed your business. But where are you now?"

20
00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:04.491
A loud cheer rose from the gathering below, but the man hardly heard it. The

21
00:02:04.492 --> 00:02:07.693
voice in his head was speaking again. "Who?

22
00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:13.248
Oh," the man said. "Yes, I can do that." This

23
00:02:13.249 --> 00:02:16.132
time when he listened, he frowned. He

24
00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.787
rose to his feet and began pacing. "I

25
00:02:19.788 --> 00:02:27.788
never fail!" he snapped. "Never! Besides, I know the perfect person to help us." Another

26
00:02:27.789 --> 00:02:33.287
brief pause followed. "Of course I know who is trustworthy. If

27
00:02:33.288 --> 00:02:37.474
you doubt my judgment, perhaps you should find someone else!" He

28
00:02:37.475 --> 00:02:44.940
listened again, his mouth curving into a slight smile. Finally he nodded. "Yes,

29
00:02:44.941 --> 00:02:55.107
I'm glad you see that." He wandered back onto the balcony and glanced at the scene below. "It's

30
00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:59.219
a deal. We shall make them all pay!" He

31
00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:14.047
laughed along with the voice in his head. "I'll begin immediately." *

32
00:03:14.048 --> 00:03:17.300
* * "See you tomorrow, Zann,"

33
00:03:17.301 --> 00:03:22.579
someone called. Zann waved without looking to see who'd spoken, and then

34
00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:27.601
stepped outside. After two months at First City Academy, he knew most of the

35
00:03:27.602 --> 00:03:31.410
kids' names. But he still didn't feel as if he had

36
00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:35.466
true friends. "Not like back home in Swamp Bottom,"

37
00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:41.021
he thought. Zann grimaced, reminding himself that Swamp Bottom wasn't

38
00:03:41.022 --> 00:03:46.762
"home" anymore. Rubbing his fingers together, he stepped away from the building and

39
00:03:46.763 --> 00:03:48.108
muttered,

40
00:03:48.109 --> 00:03:53.453
"Zap!" Splash! Zann looked around. He was standing in a neighbor's

41
00:03:53.454 --> 00:03:55.852
decorative fountain. "Drat,"

42
00:03:55.853 --> 00:03:58.923
Zann said. The neighbor was picking flutter

43
00:03:58.924 --> 00:04:01.691
flowers nearby. "Sorry," Zann said

44
00:04:01.692 --> 00:04:05.696
to her. She looked irritated for a second before her

45
00:04:05.697 --> 00:04:10.420
expression changed. "Oh, it's young Zann, the hero!"

46
00:04:10.421 --> 00:04:15.368
she exclaimed. "How are you? And how are those worlds-traveling parents

47
00:04:15.369 --> 00:04:21.273
of yours?" "Fine, thanks," Zann said politely. "Excuse me, I have

48
00:04:21.274 --> 00:04:24.965
to go." It still felt strange when people treated him like

49
00:04:24.966 --> 00:04:28.848
a celebrity. Months had passed, but it still happened all

50
00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:37.160
the time. He hurried over to his house. When he opened the front door, Zing

51
00:04:37.161 --> 00:04:40.231
flew out. The dragon chattered and

52
00:04:40.232 --> 00:04:47.028
spat flames. "Sorry I'm late," Zann told Zing. "I had to stay after school for an assembly about

53
00:04:47.029 --> 00:04:54.068
Void rights. The headmaster said that we're all supposed to work at getting along—Reds, Voids, dragons . .

54
00:04:54.069 --> 00:04:58.143
." Zann hadn't been paying much attention to the Void rights

55
00:04:58.144 --> 00:05:01.349
protests. But the assembly had made him think about

56
00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:04.789
Darb. And that made him homesick for Swamp Bottom

57
00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:11.128
again. He hadn't seen Darb for more than two months—nor their friends Perda and

58
00:05:11.129 --> 00:05:19.422
Gliss. Zing started zipping around overhead, sending flames everywhere. Zann conjured some dragon

59
00:05:19.423 --> 00:05:23.926
treats. "It's okay, boy," he called, tossing Zing the

60
00:05:23.927 --> 00:05:26.820
treats. "I know you've been stuck in the house all

61
00:05:26.821 --> 00:05:29.947
day. But now we can go to Palace Park and

62
00:05:29.948 --> 00:05:34.320
play. I just have to stop by the lab first to tell Mom and Dad where we're

63
00:05:34.321 --> 00:05:37.788
going." Zann considered sending his parents a message

64
00:05:37.789 --> 00:05:41.541
moth. Luckily, they'd stopped monitoring his every

65
00:05:41.542 --> 00:05:49.147
move. But for a month or so after Morb had been banished from Magica, Zann had had to check in with his parents all the time.

66
00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:53.203
Zann tried to grab Zing to zap them both to the lab.

67
00:05:53.204 --> 00:05:56.736
But the little dragon wouldn't hold still long enough.

68
00:05:56.737 --> 00:06:01.362
"Okay, I guess we'll walk," Zann said with a shrug.

69
00:06:01.363 --> 00:06:05.292
He headed down the street, whistling for Zing to follow.

70
00:06:05.293 --> 00:06:11.724
Zing sped past him, diving to shoot flames at a passing flip fly.

71
00:06:11.725 --> 00:06:17.872
"Hey!" A man cried, jumping aside as the flames missed the fly and almost hit him.

72
00:06:17.873 --> 00:06:21.573
"Oops," Zann called and grabbed Zing by the wing.

73
00:06:21.574 --> 00:06:25.358
"Come on, little buddy, let's take the quick way."

74
00:06:25.359 --> 00:06:26.697
Zap!

75
00:06:26.698 --> 00:06:30.902
They landed across the street from the lab where Zann's parents worked.

76
00:06:30.903 --> 00:06:38.463
Zing yanked free immediately, diving down to attack a wiggle weed growing out of a crack in the sidewalk.

77
00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:43.990
Zann hardly noticed. He stared at a group of about a dozen people.

78
00:06:43.991 --> 00:06:48.471
They were marching around in front of him holding a Void rights banner.

79
00:06:48.472 --> 00:06:52.284
Several people stood nearby and watched the marchers.

80
00:06:52.285 --> 00:06:57.274
"Not another protest!" Zann muttered, shaking his head.

81
00:06:57.275 --> 00:07:03.646
He forgot about that when he saw a message moth fluttering toward him. Zing saw it too.

82
00:07:03.647 --> 00:07:10.396
"Zing, stop!" Zann grabbed the moth before the dragon could incinerate it.

83
00:07:10.397 --> 00:07:14.868
Zann smiled when he spotted several names scrawled on one wing.

84
00:07:14.869 --> 00:07:18.308
The moth had come from his friends in Swamp Bottom!

85
00:07:18.309 --> 00:07:21.958
Before he could read their message, he heard a shout of anger.

86
00:07:21.959 --> 00:07:29.367
"Give that back, you fire-breathing thief!"

